      "worked": "For $x<0$, $\\lvert x\\rvert=-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\lvert x\\rvert-x&=-x-x\\\\\\lvert x\\rvert-x&=-2x\\ne0\\\\y&=\\frac{x}{-2x}\\\\y&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x\\ge0$, $\\lvert x\\rvert=x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\lvert x\\rvert-x&=x-x\\\\\\lvert x\\rvert-x&=0\\end{align*}$$\nDivision by zero is undefined, so\n$$y=\\begin{cases}-\\dfrac12&\\text{if }x<0,\\\\\\text{undefined}&\\text{if }x\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$\nEquivalently, $y=-\\frac12$ on the domain $(-\\infty,0)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
